---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — RigPure"
  description="How RigPure collects, uses and protects your personal data, the legal bases we rely on, and your rights under the GDPR."
>
  <div class="article-wrap"><div class="container">
    <article class="prose" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: August 24, 2026</em></p>

      <div class="callout warn">
        <span class="c-label">Note</span>
        <p>This is a template and must be reviewed by a qualified lawyer and completed with your company details before publication.</p>
      </div>

      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how [Company / Publisher name] ("we", "us", "RigPure") collects, uses and protects your personal data when you visit rigpure.com (the "Site"). We are committed to processing your data in accordance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and applicable data protection laws.</p>

      <h2>Data controller</h2>
      <p>The data controller responsible for your personal data is:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>[Company / Publisher name]</strong></li>
        <li>[Address]</li>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:contact@rigpure.com">contact@rigpure.com</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect the following categories of data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Usage and analytics data:</strong> pages viewed, time spent, referring pages, approximate location (country/region), device type, browser and operating system, collected through our analytics tool.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising identifiers and cookies:</strong> identifiers set by advertising cookies to serve and measure ads, and — where you consent — to personalise them.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address (which may be truncated/anonymised), and log data generated automatically by your browser.</li>
        <li><strong>Data you provide directly:</strong> for example, if you contact us by email, the content of your message and your contact details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Purposes of processing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Operating, securing and maintaining the Site;</li>
        <li>Measuring audience and understanding how the Site is used (analytics);</li>
        <li>Displaying advertising and measuring its performance;</li>
        <li>Personalising advertising (only with your consent);</li>
        <li>Responding to your requests and messages.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Legal bases</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR): for non-essential cookies, audience measurement, and personalised advertising. You may withdraw consent at any time.</li>
        <li><strong>Legitimate interest</strong> (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR): for keeping the Site secure, preventing abuse, and basic operation. You may object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
        <li><strong>Performance of a contract or pre-contractual steps / legal obligation</strong> where applicable.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third parties and recipients</h2>
      <p>We share data with the following categories of service providers and partners, who process it on our behalf or as independent controllers:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google AdSense and advertising partners:</strong> to serve, cap and measure advertising. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">how Google uses data</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics provider:</strong> [Analytics tool name, e.g. Google Analytics / Plausible] to measure audience.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting and infrastructure:</strong> Cloudflare, Inc.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your personal data.</p>

      <h2>International data transfers</h2>
      <p>Some of our providers are located outside the European Economic Area (for example in the United States). Where data is transferred internationally, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses or applicable adequacy frameworks.</p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>We keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described above:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Analytics data: [e.g. up to 14 months];</li>
        <li>Advertising cookie data: for the lifetime of the relevant cookies (see our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>);</li>
        <li>Email correspondence: [e.g. up to 3 years] after the last contact.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Subject to applicable law, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li><strong>Rectify</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data;</li>
        <li><strong>Erase</strong> your data ("right to be forgotten");</li>
        <li><strong>Restrict</strong> or <strong>object</strong> to processing, including processing based on legitimate interest and direct marketing;</li>
        <li><strong>Data portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format;</li>
        <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to exercise your rights</h2>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@rigpure.com">contact@rigpure.com</a> (or our Data Protection Officer at [DPO email], if appointed). We may need to verify your identity before responding. We will reply within the timeframe required by law (generally one month).</p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you believe your data protection rights have been infringed, you have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, in particular in the EU Member State of your residence, place of work or the place of the alleged infringement ([relevant supervisory authority, e.g. CNIL in France]).</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>Detailed information about the cookies we use and how to manage them is available in our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the latest revision.</p>
    </article>
  </div></div>
</BaseLayout>
